I’m leveraging what I’ve learned. I need to get some candidates for those gaps to refine them and continue pushing the convergence, and I’m going to do this through the *Surrogate-Inverse Model (SIM)*, since the parameter count, f2, is monotonic with many variables, meaning a Ridge Regression from F -> X is robust. I’ll also use *Directed Local Search* and perturb the best solutions to really squeeze out hypervolume. Finally, I'll use *Boundary Targeting* to specifically aim for 19.5M-19.6M with heavy skip connection reinforcement to hopefully keep things stable.

